      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case of a 42-year-old woman with a right coronary artery fistula into the right ventricle is reported; she was asymptomatic and a continuous precordial murmur was found on physical examination. We discuss the usefulness and limitation of the Echo 2-D/Doppler findings, concerning this diagnosis, which was only definitively established by angiocardiography."},
